      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2023-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Group into pairs \\((2k)^3-(2k-1)^3\\) for \\(k=1,\\ldots,9.\\) Expanding, \\[ \\begin{gathered} (2k)^3-(2k-1)^3\\\\ {}=12k^2-6k+1. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nSumming for \\(k=1\\) to \\(9,\\) with \\(\\sum k^2=285\\) and \\(\\sum k=45,\\) gives \\[ \\begin{gathered} 12\\cdot 285-6\\cdot 45+9\\\\ {}=3420-270+9\\\\ {}=3159. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
